# Git push & deploy — explicit only

Never commit, push, or deploy unless the user clearly asks in that message.

## Commands

| User says | Do |
|---|---|
| **push** | `git push` only (commit first only if they also asked to commit, or there is already a commit to push) |
| **push and deploy** / **push & deploy** / **deploy** | Push (if needed) **and** deploy to the VPS |
| **commit** | Commit only — do not push or deploy |
| Anything else / silent | Do **not** commit, push, or deploy |

## Hard rules

- **Do not deploy** unless the user says **deploy** (alone or with push).
- Finishing a feature is **not** permission to push or deploy.
- Do not “helpfully” push/deploy after commits.
- If unclear whether they want deploy, ask — do not deploy.
